files.thing.webapp/section.domain/entity.Relat:
id: S.webapp.due
kind: requirement
fields:
  thing: thing.webapp
  title: Due dates
  text: the app must use local calendar dates in the owner's IANA time zone. The anchor must be the latest qualifying event date, or the goal creation date when none exists. dueDate must equal anchor plus intervalDays. A goal must become due when today's date reaches dueDate, unless paused or snoozed until a later date. Revising a goal must not create a ContactEvent. Date and time-zone fixtures must cover daylight-saving changes.
  enabled: true
  source:
    doc: keep-in-touch-world-specification
    section: "6"
links:
  - { rel: subject, to: entity.RelationshipGoal }
  - { rel: subject, to: entity.Suggestion }
  - { rel: subject, to: operation.goal.save }
  - { rel: refines, to: GD.goals }
  - { rel: refines, to: GD.prompts }

id: S.webapp.qualification
kind: requirement
fields:
  thing: thing.webapp
  title: Goal qualification
  text: an enabled goal must have intervalDays from 1 through 3650 and desiredDepth in light, meaningful or shared-time. These are the owner's labels, not a global quality ranking. A ContactEvent must qualify only when the owner explicitly marks that it met this goal. The app must record the goal ID and desiredDepth at confirmation and count only qualifications matching the current desiredDepth. Changing depth may change which historical events qualify; SchedulePreview must show that effect before saving. Editing or deleting an event must recompute the schedule.
  enabled: true
  source:
    doc: keep-in-touch-world-specification
    section: "6"
links:
  - { rel: subject, to: entity.RelationshipGoal }
  - { rel: subject, to: entity.ContactEvent }
  - { rel: subject, to: component.SchedulePreview }
  - { rel: subject, to: operation.contact.log }
  - { rel: refines, to: GD.goals }
  - { rel: refines, to: GD.prompts }

